    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **277 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the daily owner-creation cap on `POST /api/owners`: once 20 owners already have a registration date of today, the 21st creation attempt is rejected with **400 Bad Request**.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, I added:\n\n1. **`EnforceDailyOwnerLimit`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 reads the candidate owner via `@Val Owner`, counts existing owners with the same registration date (defaulting to today) through `OwnerRepository.findAll()`, and throws when the count is already at the cap (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 20`). Since it runs before `save` within the request transaction, it counts only owners created earlier.\n\n2. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`** \u2014 a checked exception (so it appears in the `throws` clause and OfficeFloor routes it as an escalation).\n\n3. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededExceptionHandler`** + its escalation YAML \u2014 responds with a `ProblemDetail` at status 400, mirroring the existing `OwnerAlreadyExistsException` handler.\n\n4. Wired the new `enforceDailyLimit` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `ensureUnique` and `assignMembership`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the surrounding steps.\n\nThe new `Cp13Tests` passes (20 creations succeed, the 21st returns 400), and no existing tests regressed.",
